1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:51,676
<i>The siblings lost their parents</i>

3
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,304
<i>when their home collapsed</i>
<i>in a government air strike.</i>

4
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,057
<i>They moved in with relatives,</i>

5
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:00,143
<i>but civil war forced them to flee again.</i>

6
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:03,855
Don't let go of my hand,
Neema, so you don't fall.

7
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:07,025
<i>All alone, after struggling to survive,</i>

8
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:10,403
<i>wandering the streets aimlessly,</i>
<i>evading soldiers and robbers,</i>

9
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,114
<i>- and scavenging through the ruins…</i>
- How did you find that?

10
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,658
Have some water.

11
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:19,162
<i>…the two children</i>
<i>eventually collapsed from malnutrition.</i>

12
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>And, even as they lay there,</i>
<i>they held hands,</i>

13
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:24,751
<i>not giving up on each other.</i>

14
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:26,169
REGULAR DONATIONS INQUIRIES
30,000 WON PER MONTH

15
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:30,340
<i>Likewise, the White Wings Medical Corps</i>
<i>didn't give up on them either.</i>

16
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:35,512
Does it hurt?

17
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:36,971
<i>Dr. Kim Seung-hyo,</i>

18
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:39,307
<i>once one of the world's</i>
<i>leading general surgeons</i>

19
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:41,601
<i>and a professor</i>
<i>at a prestigious medical school,</i>

20
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:44,187
<i>left all of his wealth and fame behind</i>

21
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:47,690
<i>to found the White Wings Medical Corps</i>
<i>and settled here in Lagota.</i>

22
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,819
<i>His daughter also became a doctor,</i>

23
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:53,321
<i>and despite her efforts</i>
<i>to bring him back to Korea,</i>

24
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:56,366
<i>he left everything behind</i>
<i>and headed to Lagota.</i>

25
00:01:57,242 --> 00:02:01,204
<i>For Dr. Kim, who lives a frugal life,</i>
<i>these drawings from the children</i>

26
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:04,207
<i>are held as his greatest treasure and joy.</i>

27
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,458
Baba.

28
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:08,128
<i>The children refer to Dr. Kim as "Baba."</i>

29
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:12,006
<i>Lagota's Baba, the white-coat hero.</i>

30
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:16,511
<i>However, Baba, Dr. Kim Seung-hyo,</i>
<i>can't do this alone.</i>

31
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:17,887
- Patient coming through!
- Clear the way!

32
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,681
<i>The civil war is still ongoing.</i>

33
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:22,684
<i>They face a severe shortage</i>
<i>of all medical supplies.</i>

34
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:26,729
<i>Baba Kim Seung-hyo himself</i>
<i>recently had to undergo a heart transplant</i>

35
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:28,815
<i>under extremely substandard conditions.</i>

36
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:32,527
<i>All of the children</i>
<i>prayed their hardest for Baba.</i>

37
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,445
Baba! Baba!

38
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,865
<i>Please help the children of Lagota.</i>

39
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,199
30,000 WON PER MONTH

40
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:40,285
<i>Please become a baba to these children.</i>

41
00:02:40,368 --> 00:02:42,412
FOOD FOR MALNUTRITION PROVIDED
SAVING 290,000 CHILDREN EACH YEAR

42
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,289
<i>Please help these children keep smiling.</i>

43
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,543
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

44
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:51,254
Okay, let's go.

45
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:53,006
Time to go outside.

46
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:55,008
EPISODE 11

47
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:56,676
- Neema. Open.
- Good job.

48
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:57,760
Ah!

49
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:04,184
Miss Teacher.

50
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:06,519
Mm?

51
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:09,439
Is Baba good? A good person?

52
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:12,650
Right.

53
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,613
He saved you, Neema,

54
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:18,990
and your friends.

55
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:20,658
He teaches you, too.

56
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,411
You said that yourself.

57
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,836
Good? What about me?

58
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:33,463
Good too?

59
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,256
Uh-uh!

60
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:40,637
Baraka! Baraka!

61
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,685
Na-gyeong!

62
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:52,023
It doesn't look like
my family at all, does it?

63
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,107
MY FAMILY
MOM, DAD, KIM WON-JIN

64
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:55,401
Wow, I guess
I'm really terrible at drawing.

65
00:03:56,945 --> 00:04:00,114
Won-jin, your dad's
a big doctor, isn't he?

66
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:01,699
Yeah.

67
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:04,994
Did you ever play doctor
with your dad too?

68
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:06,955
No, I don't get to.

69
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:09,332
I touched his stethoscope once
a long time ago,

70
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,668
and mom yelled at me really bad for it.

71
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:15,797
Also, my dad's way too busy
to play with me anyways.

72
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:19,008
No matter how great of a doctor he is…

73
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,219
Hey! Where are you going?

74
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:24,222
Na-gyeong! Hey, Na-gyeong!

75
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:29,102
HAPPINESS KINDERGARTEN

76
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:42,490
PLAYING DOCTOR
PARK TAE-GYEONG

77
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:52,125
Now, shall you and I
go play doctor together?

78
00:04:56,921 --> 00:05:00,550
PLAYING DOCTOR
PARK TAE-GYEONG

79
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:15,898
No!

80
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,506
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

81
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:44,302
Dr. Yoon from Cardiothoracic and Dr. Shim
from Cardiology will be here today.

82
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,678
Been forever, huh?

83
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:48,222
It's rare for so many departments
to get together like this.

84
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:53,770
They say it's always hard going
into briefings on organ donation surgery.

85
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:55,438
It is, right?

86
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:58,483
Ah, on the subject of
heart transplant surgery,

87
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:01,944
I've heard Dr. Kim Seung-hyo
personally requested Gye Su-jeong.

88
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:05,114
- Apparently, she did his first transplant.
- What, are you serious?

89
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,617
Who in the world is Gye Su-jeong?
I mean, really!

90
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,828
I heard he wanted Jo Won-jin
as the anesthesiologist, as well.

91
00:06:13,289 --> 00:06:14,832
Uh, Director, were you already aware,

92
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,335
that Doctor Jo Won-jin's
actually Dr. Kim's daughter?

93
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:20,713
I didn't know. It was news to me.

94
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:23,049
Wow, not even you were aware.

95
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:25,343
I was curious how those two were related.

96
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:28,221
I think I might ask her casually,
when I see her.

97
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:30,890
Her name was Kim Won-jin,
but she changed it to Jo Won-jin.

98
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:32,767
Everyone's all curious and chatty now.

99
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,602
I'm sure she had her own reasons.

100
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:36,229
Since this is a redo dissection,

101
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:38,648
I think I'll need to coordinate
the timing of the heart surgery.

102
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:40,525
Ah, yes, I'll take care of it.

103
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:54,038
Whoa, what's with everyone's faces?
I don't think I can ask her.

104
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:56,707
Park Tae-gyeong isn't even here.

105
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:58,709
Go on.

106
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:05,925
You're a trooper, Hyeon-a, I mean it.

107
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:09,387
Ah, it seems to be healing well.

108
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,889
Dr. Gye Su-jeong
was just here with us earlier,

109
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,599
and she told us the same thing.

110
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,810
Oh, good to hear.

111
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:19,230
Thank you for everything.

112
00:07:19,313 --> 00:07:21,858
Oh! No, I couldn't.
You should keep it, Hyeon-a.

113
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:24,026
It was a very nice gift
from Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

114
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:27,363
- I have so many already.
- Oh, wow, it would appear so.

115
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:28,614
You're very lucky.

116
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:29,991
Um, excuse me.

117
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:33,786
That one famous doctor
who started that relief mission, uh…

118
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:37,290
Dr. Kim Seung-hyo. That's the one.

119
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,709
Yes, him.

120
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:43,379
Nowadays, Hyeon-a's dream is to become
a doctor like Dr. Gye Su-jeong,

121
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,673
but she used to want to be
like Kim Seung-hyo,

122
00:07:45,756 --> 00:07:48,176
- that's what she always used to say.
- I even saved up my allowance

123
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:50,303
to send Baba a text message!

124
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,856
Rock, paper, scissors… I win!

125
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,941
<i>Hyeon-a really wants to meet him.</i>

126
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,943
<i>She says he's a great doctor</i>

127
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,529
<i>who lives to help sick children</i>
<i>in faraway places.</i>

128
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,990
<i>She wants to cheer him on</i>
<i>and wish him a fast recovery.</i>

129
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:23,044
Before we eat, shall we play doctor?

130
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:34,430
You know you can't tell
Mom and Dad about this, right?

131
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:38,351
Today… you'll be the doctor.

132
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,910
Young doctor?

133
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:57,578
Oh…

134
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,580
Heading to lunch soon, aren't you?

135
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:03,125
Oh, no, I'm okay. I should be going.

136
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,003
I wanted to say,

137
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:08,714
I'm the one who took
Dr. Gye to Kim Seung-hyo.

138
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:18,558
I wanted to brag a little…

139
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:25,565
show that legendary doctor
I trained an excellent, talented student.

140
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:29,694
I wanted to teach her so many things,

141
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,488
but the results of that
followed us all the way here.

142
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,284
Now, knowing that,

143
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:39,412
will you condemn me, Doctor?

144
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,957
Won't you get mad at Jang Hui-suk,

145
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,876
the proud, arrogant fool,
instead of Gye Su-jeong,

146
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:49,005
who constantly wakes from nightmares,

147
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:50,965
too scared to read that kid's letters?

148
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:08,149
He was my parents' oldest friend.

149
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:10,985
They stuck together
and they always trusted him.

150
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:14,071
Because of the new hospital
he was building,

151
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:17,283
he lived with us for about a year or so.

152
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:22,121
If I go by what you said, Ms. Jang,

153
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,915
my parents are the ones
who told that man to come and stay,

154
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,837
so the ones I should get upset with
are my parents.

155
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:34,550
But I know my parents
aren't responsible for what he did.

156
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:37,970
Even I know that much.

157
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:01,744
Oh! Auntie, I actually
had something to tell you.

158
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:04,455
That patient with the epidermoid cyst,
did you do the surgery?

159
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:06,374
You mean you saw that?

160
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:08,626
Oh man, I had to scoop out
the tumor with a cup,

161
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,670
- I wish you could've seen me.
- A cup?

162
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,838
Have you gone insane?

163
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:15,591
Well, Baba said he would do it like that

164
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:17,718
- back in the day.
- What, are you joking?

165
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:21,305
That patient had never been able to
sleep lying down because of the tumor.

166
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,516
And, thanks to me, now he actually can.

167
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:25,226
Do you have any idea how much he suffered?

168
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:27,895
I heard he lost consciousness
from all the bleeding and pain.

169
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:31,857
He's got terminal cancer anyway,

170
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:34,443
so we decided that was
the least we could do for him here.

171
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:37,988
Dr. Kim wanting him added to the Doctor X
database couldn't be the reason for it?

172
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,784
What's wrong? Come on, Auntie,
it's a new method for--

173
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,912
Did the epidermoid cyst get triaged?
Sure that's what it is?

174
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:48,165
- I saw it in the database.
- And was that for the patient's sake?

175
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:52,253
You're sure you weren't just curious?

176
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:54,088
Wanting to see
whether you could do it or not,

177
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:56,882
what the tumor would look like,
what would happen if you cut it open,

178
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,552
how far you can take a surgery
without applying anesthesia?

179
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,054
Uh…

180
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:07,017
- I'm sorry, Auntie, that's not what--
- You need to ask yourself, honestly,

181
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:11,689
as to whether that surgery sincerely was
for your patient, or for your own sake.

182
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:39,008
My teacher, is… really angry with me.

183
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:40,092
Why?

184
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:42,720
Mmm…

185
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,811
I suppose I've become a…

186
00:12:53,481 --> 00:12:54,690
…monster.

187
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:57,526
You're not a monster.
Doctor, you're not a monster!

188
00:12:58,819 --> 00:13:00,070
Baraka.

189
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:04,492
A monster shoots, a monster bombs,
a monster is an airplane.

190
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:07,703
Su-jeong's not a monster. No!

191
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,749
My dream? To be a doctor.

192
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:16,796
Gye Su-jeong is my dream.
To become a doctor.

193
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:15,855
You can go inside.

194
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,317
He's sleeping,
he won't know anyone's there.

195
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:23,487
Oh, it's okay, thank you.

196
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:29,660
You heard, didn't you?

197
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:35,583
Park Tae-gyeong, and his attempted murder.

198
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,128
Dr. Gye saved his life
just in time, again.

199
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:47,261
I stood by and watched as he did it.

200
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,686
So, then, this is the badge
of honor you earned yourself

201
00:14:55,769 --> 00:14:58,063
saving those children in that fire.

202
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:02,526
The great big, so-called "angel's mark".

203
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:06,906
Or, so everybody else still thinks.

204
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,922
Dr. Gye Su-jeong?

205
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:51,659
It's been a while, Dr. Kim.

206
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,870
Park Tae-gyeong?

207
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:58,457
It's Tae-gyeong.
Director Park Yun-il's son.

208
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:02,544
I thought you might've forgotten me,
so I took some of my old drawings along.

209
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:04,755
Wanna take a look?

210
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:12,596
Together with you,
I drew in my sketchbook,

211
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,139
practiced my writing.

212
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,858
You told me to properly destroy it
because it was our secret,

213
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,904
but I hid it instead,
because I couldn't get rid of it.

214
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:34,201
You said if I told on you, you wouldn't
help my parents if they got sick.

215
00:16:34,284 --> 00:16:36,870
So I didn't tell anyone what you did.

216
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:49,967
I even drew us together, playing doctor.

217
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:55,097
Did you play doctor with your dad?

218
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:05,899
Na-gyeong!

219
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:14,241
Na-gyeong.

220
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:25,085
Don't. Listen, you can quit the drugs.

221
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:28,505
I told you the other day,
when we first reconnected,

222
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:29,923
back there in the ER.

223
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:34,470
Now that we're in touch again,
you can quit your addiction. Okay?

224
00:17:34,553 --> 00:17:35,763
Okay?

225
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,976
Come down. Okay?

226
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,061
You don't…

227
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:45,272
Why won't you believe me, Won-jin?

228
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:47,024
Na-gyeong, that's…

229
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:51,403
You… Get here quickly. Please!
We're on the roof.

230
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,031
It's… It's not a hallucination.

231
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,159
We… We played…

232
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:58,869
doctor.

233
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,333
<i>Every time I slept over at your place,</i>

234
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:08,545
<i>he gave me presents. </i>

235
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:11,965
Shall we go to that room now?

236
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:14,676
<i>And said it was a secret,</i>

237
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,221
and he made me swear not to say anything.

238
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:20,057
O-Okay, okay, I understand. Hello?

239
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,059
Just get here, please! Come right now!

240
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:23,560
Later, your mother…

241
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:27,606
wrote a check to my mother
so she wouldn't talk.

242
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:29,817
What?

243
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,401
Your dad…

244
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:34,780
they all say he's a godsend,

245
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:36,490
that he's an angel.

246
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:39,576
Na-gyeong…

247
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:42,412
Look, it's because of the drugs.
It's because of the drugs.

248
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:43,622
- You're mentally not--
- Won-jin.

249
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:47,960
I…

250
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:53,507
feel so lucky we reunited
after so long apart.

251
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:56,552
Yeah. I agree. I feel the same.

252
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,638
So, then… Here, let's head inside.

253
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,640
Because now I can show you.

254
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:04,977
Watch closely.

255
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:07,312
Your dad is…

256
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:11,024
a monster.

257
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:50,647
My dad told me years ago that
whenever a donor would finally appear,

258
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:53,233
you'd come here to get your transplant.

259
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:56,195
That's why I came to this hospital.

260
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,823
Because there was one thing
I really wanted to ask you.

261
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:06,622
Dr. Kim?

262
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:24,681
He looks so at peace.

263
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,743
Hello, ma'am. Are you… Are you okay?

264
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:29,788
Huh? Ms. Jang! Hold on, get up.

265
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:32,791
What's wrong, are you hurt? Huh?

266
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,668
Let's get you to the ER first.
I'll bring you there.

267
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:38,505
- It's all right.
- Ah… No, no, no, no, no.

268
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:41,425
I've never walked away from a patient
who clearly needs to be treated.

269
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,760
You can barely even breathe,
where do you think you're going?

270
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,387
Come on, lean on me.

271
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:50,600
Oh, Dr. Kim. You're a really good doctor.

272
00:21:50,684 --> 00:21:53,437
Oh, me? I have to be, don't I?

273
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:56,606
Then, with that,
lean on this good doctor, let's go.

274
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:58,442
I believe it was just
a little hyperventilation,

275
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:00,444
though you can't be too careful.

276
00:22:00,527 --> 00:22:01,528
Hold on.

277
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:03,947
Here, Dr. Kim, this is for you.

278
00:22:05,866 --> 00:22:06,992
Uh, what's this?

279
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,744
That belongs to you today, Doctor.

280
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,954
Please continue to take good care
of your patients,

281
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:13,248
- and enjoy the food.
- Oh… I just…

282
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:15,334
I mean, the ER's closed,
there's no patients here…

283
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:17,419
- I don't know if I deserve--
- Good day, Doctor.

284
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:19,087
- I…
- Hmm.

285
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,589
Uh, are you sure you're okay?

286
00:22:43,278 --> 00:22:45,447
You're holding on with painkillers anyway,

287
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:49,201
so you probably can't hear anything,
and won't remember what happened.

288
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,000
I just wish that we could do the same.

289
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:14,309
Why… Why are you looking at me like that?

290
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:17,104
Dr. Gye?

291
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:20,357
Are there…

292
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,569
Are there actually other children?

293
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:56,935
- Oh, Ms. Jang!
- You're home.

294
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:59,354
Oh! Eung-gu, can you bring some water?

295
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:01,648
- Sure.
- What about Su-jeong?

296
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:03,733
I didn't meet with her.

297
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:07,362
So you opted not to?
It's not that you couldn't?

298
00:24:12,325 --> 00:24:14,536
Seeing that intern and Dr. Jo,

299
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:18,206
I just couldn't summon the strength
to meet with her, I was too exhausted.

300
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:22,335
Lord.

301
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:25,088
Here. Wow!

302
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,841
Wow!

303
00:24:28,467 --> 00:24:29,301
Whoa.

304
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:35,765
This is too big a portion.
There's no way I can eat all this.

305
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,310
Looks to me like we've got
a feast fit to feed you

306
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:40,479
along with several other people, at least.

307
00:24:42,856 --> 00:24:44,900
Wow, something's gotta be wrong.

308
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:47,444
You're never this composed
in front of food like this.

309
00:24:47,527 --> 00:24:50,113
I have to assume something's going on.

310
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,198
Well, you'd be wrong.

311
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:52,908
Whoa, did you just
pick up your chopsticks?

312
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:55,327
You're picking at it
and not using a spoon to wolf it down?

313
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:59,498
This really isn't adding up.
It's not like you. What's going on?

314
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,877
It's okay. No, no.
I-I was just teasing you.

315
00:25:03,960 --> 00:25:06,171
Your shift ended forever ago
but you're still here,

316
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:08,965
just wandering about
like a poor stray cat.

317
00:25:09,049 --> 00:25:11,718
So, as the cat mom I am in my heart,
I had to rescue you,

318
00:25:11,801 --> 00:25:14,262
and give you a bit of che-ow. Meow!

319
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:18,642
Right, sorry. Eat up. Here.

320
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:26,608
Hey, so, earlier, Ms. Jang was
swaying on her feet outside the lobby.

321
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:29,236
Just hyperventilating.

322
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:31,571
She was all…

323
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:35,158
But, luckily, it didn't last long.
She got better and left just fine, but…

324
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:37,744
Mm…

325
00:25:39,955 --> 00:25:41,081
Hey, you know…

326
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:44,501
just another ordinary doctor like me

327
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:47,254
could never understand
how you and Ms. Jang

328
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:50,590
climbed up from hardship,
and got yourselves to where you are now.

329
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:53,760
And No-fun Won-jin, Jo Won-jin,
was actually Kim Won-jin.

330
00:25:53,843 --> 00:25:54,970
How could she not let me in on that?

331
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:57,347
I feel like I'm really being
excluded here, you know?

332
00:25:59,224 --> 00:26:02,352
Anyway, Park Tae-gyeong,
that sunshiny dimwit,

333
00:26:02,435 --> 00:26:04,688
I have no idea why he vanished
from your little group, Dr. Gye.

334
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:10,485
But I do happen to see…

335
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:14,656
you're trying your hardest,
not to break down,

336
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:16,408
while things are looking really dark.

337
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:25,166
Seeing the food she prepared,
I can already tell.

338
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:27,460
The feeling she must have,

339
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:29,629
of wanting to help you endure
by making this for you,

340
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:31,673
and her own wish to overcome this.

341
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:34,968
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

342
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:41,808
Please don't break down.
If only for Director Jang.

343
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:44,894
Wow.

344
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:48,523
This rice is very labor-intensive
to make, you know?

345
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:50,108
Super healthy, too, right?

346
00:26:50,191 --> 00:26:52,027
Mmm, mmm!

347
00:26:52,110 --> 00:26:53,737
Pot rice. It's pot rice, right?

348
00:26:53,820 --> 00:26:55,488
Mm.

349
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:59,159
Oh, No-fun Won-jin and Tae-gyeong
The Vanishing should've joined us too.

350
00:26:59,701 --> 00:27:01,202
Man, where did they go?

351
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:08,126
ONYU NURSING HOSPITAL

352
00:27:20,889 --> 00:27:23,058
It's funny, she doesn't throw that photo.

353
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:24,643
She wipes it every day.

354
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:27,520
Even though she forgets and drops things
because of her dementia,

355
00:27:27,604 --> 00:27:29,522
she never messes with that photo.

356
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,733
Isn't that amazing?

357
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:35,945
Come by more often.
You don't visit nearly enough.

358
00:27:53,213 --> 00:27:55,465
How could you do something like that?

359
00:27:55,548 --> 00:27:57,967
How could I? How could he?

360
00:27:58,051 --> 00:28:00,887
How could he!

361
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:07,310
After I found out,
your dad stopped doing that.

362
00:28:07,394 --> 00:28:10,271
And I went to apologize
to Na-gyeong's family,

363
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:12,232
and her mother
asked for some money, and I--

364
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:15,652
Are you serious?
You're pretending it's all okay?

365
00:28:18,613 --> 00:28:20,198
It-It's because Dad has a…

366
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:23,284
peculiar disease.

367
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:25,370
A… A what?

368
00:28:25,453 --> 00:28:29,916
He said to me it had been given
to him by the Lord, to test him.

369
00:28:29,999 --> 00:28:32,502
- That's what he said? It's a "test"?
- Mm-hmm.

370
00:28:32,585 --> 00:28:34,587
Your father is an angel, Won-jin.

371
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,423
Even now, he's out there,
somewhere far away,

372
00:28:36,506 --> 00:28:37,924
helping those who are suffering,

373
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:40,885
all for free,
because it's his life's work!

374
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:43,054
He is a good shepherd to the lost sheep.

375
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:44,681
Dad is a monster!

376
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:49,269
He's a monster, the worst kind.

377
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:53,064
Won-jin…

378
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:55,817
how are you able to…

379
00:28:57,610 --> 00:28:59,195
talk about your Dad like that?

380
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,822
He doesn't do that anymore.

381
00:29:00,905 --> 00:29:03,408
You hear me? He's done! That's it!

382
00:29:07,328 --> 00:29:08,747
Tell me, have you ever thought…

383
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:12,667
maybe your dad did that
so you wouldn't test his strength?

384
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,128
So you didn't get hurt? Have you?

385
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:30,560
You know what?

386
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,271
Mom…

387
00:29:36,399 --> 00:29:38,651
You're a monster, just like Dad.

388
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:42,071
We'll never be a family again,
like we were in that picture.

389
00:29:44,073 --> 00:29:45,909
You're not my parents,
I'm not your daughter.

390
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,624
Why did you come here
instead of going to the police?

391
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:56,419
You could've told them the kind of person
you believe your dad is,

392
00:29:56,503 --> 00:29:57,754
so why'd you come here?

393
00:30:01,841 --> 00:30:04,719
'Cause in reality,
you want to believe your dad, too.

394
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:07,263
Won-jin. Hey.

395
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:09,557
Now that we see things clearly,
and know the truth,

396
00:30:09,641 --> 00:30:11,100
we just need to believe it.

397
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:13,812
Huh? Won-jin!

398
00:30:44,884 --> 00:30:51,850
INTERN KIM WON-JIN

399
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:14,873
Oh, for goodness' sake.

400
00:31:14,956 --> 00:31:16,749
I should charge the hospital
an overnight fee.

401
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:18,042
Working this late…

402
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:19,419
Oh my.

403
00:31:19,502 --> 00:31:21,129
You didn't take an umbrella?

404
00:31:21,212 --> 00:31:22,463
Ah, gosh…

405
00:31:23,172 --> 00:31:25,425
What about dinner? Have you eaten?

406
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,304
You're…

407
00:31:31,097 --> 00:31:33,641
Come here. Goodness, you're soaked.

408
00:31:39,314 --> 00:31:40,857
I have a question.

409
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:42,525
Why did you take me in, Auntie?

410
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:45,028
Are you really asking?

411
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:50,033
No, this won't do. Go change right now.

412
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:52,785
I'll make you some hot ginger tea
in the meantime.

413
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:55,079
You'll catch a cold, eh? Go on.

414
00:31:57,999 --> 00:31:59,000
Well?

415
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:02,211
You're not even my real auntie.

416
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:07,675
I asked your mother that question
back in the day.

417
00:32:09,010 --> 00:32:12,639
"Hey, sis, why did you
take me in like you did?

418
00:32:13,514 --> 00:32:15,016
We aren't even real sisters."

419
00:32:17,393 --> 00:32:19,187
Well, how did she respond?

420
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:21,731
Your mother said, "Oh, I don't know.

421
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:25,318
From the moment that I first saw you,
all I could think about

422
00:32:25,401 --> 00:32:29,238
was taking you home
and running a warm bath for you,

423
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:31,658
giving you something hot to eat,

424
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:35,036
and putting you to bed
in a nice and comfy, toasty room."

425
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:37,080
Something like that.

426
00:32:37,163 --> 00:32:38,706
I couldn't understand it. But…

427
00:32:41,084 --> 00:32:42,961
then, I was late that day…

428
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,172
<i>the day of her funeral.</i>

429
00:32:46,255 --> 00:32:47,882
THE LATE KANG IN-OK
CHIEF MOURNER GYE SU-JEONG

430
00:32:51,594 --> 00:32:54,138
<i>And just like her, all those years ago,</i>

431
00:32:54,222 --> 00:32:56,933
<i>all I could think about then</i>
<i>was taking you home,</i>

432
00:32:57,016 --> 00:32:58,977
<i>running a warm bath for you,</i>

433
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:03,106
giving you something hot to eat,
and putting you to bed in a toasty room.

434
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:05,942
That's how it was.

435
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:08,111
That's how it turned out.

436
00:33:16,077 --> 00:33:17,328
That's the same way I felt.

437
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:21,541
About Baraka,

438
00:33:23,751 --> 00:33:24,752
Neema,

439
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:30,216
and every kid I knew back in those days…

440
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:45,898
Amazing work on the bulgogi.

441
00:34:39,827 --> 00:34:42,663
Dr. Kim's not here, I'm afraid,
he's getting tests done.

442
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:43,998
Mm, all right.

443
00:34:44,082 --> 00:34:46,709
Every day, he'd talk about
how he missed you so much.

444
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:51,631
I've seen you in some pictures,
but you resemble him even more in person.

445
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:57,196
Is something wrong?

446
00:35:58,447 --> 00:36:00,074
This is what you saw?

447
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:01,826
The album you found back then.

448
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:04,203
You're sure?

449
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:30,688
Doctor Jo. Would you…
Would you, uh, happen…

450
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:38,821
He brought this here? How…

451
00:36:40,031 --> 00:36:41,699
How dare he do this!

452
00:36:47,455 --> 00:36:49,999
- It's Dr. Gye.
- Dr. Gye!

453
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:54,378
Hi!

454
00:36:57,548 --> 00:36:58,549
Hyeon-a…

455
00:37:00,134 --> 00:37:02,845
said she'd been wanting to
come meet him before she goes,

456
00:37:07,433 --> 00:37:09,227
so he invited her to visit.

457
00:37:15,149 --> 00:37:16,150
Uh, Dr. Gye…

458
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:23,199
I…

459
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:25,451
Just for me…

460
00:37:29,372 --> 00:37:31,791
Uh, can't you please just fail this once?

461
00:37:37,672 --> 00:37:39,131
Uh, c-could you…

462
00:37:40,967 --> 00:37:43,135
Can you please just fail this one surgery?

463
00:38:16,002 --> 00:38:17,336
<i>Hi, Neema.</i>

464
00:38:18,546 --> 00:38:21,716
<i>I'm sorry about not replying</i>
<i>to your letters for so long.</i>

465
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:26,137
<i>I couldn't muster up the courage</i>
<i>to write back to you.</i>

466
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:33,769
<i>The truth is…</i>

467
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:36,564
<i>I'm a coward…</i>

468
00:38:37,565 --> 00:38:40,192
<i>I don't even have the courage</i>
<i>to read your letters.</i>

469
00:38:42,361 --> 00:38:45,781
<i>However, I'm always thinking about you.</i>

470
00:38:45,865 --> 00:38:47,867
<i>I always wonder how you are.</i>

471
00:38:50,244 --> 00:38:53,664
<i>Neema. What do you like to do now?</i>

472
00:38:55,916 --> 00:38:57,710
<i>What songs do you sing?</i>

473
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,504
<i>Does Baraka…</i>

474
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:03,466
<i>come to you in your dreams?</i>

475
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:07,261
Miss Teacher!

476
00:39:08,596 --> 00:39:09,847
Neema!

477
00:39:14,894 --> 00:39:18,397
Wow! This is so cute, Neema.

478
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:23,819
Baraka was bad, he did a no-no.

479
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:27,239
Mmm? Baraka's gonna get in trouble.

480
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:32,370
At night, every day, he goes to Baba,
but he's not getting better.

481
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:36,248
To Baba? Every day? Night?

482
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,543
They go play.

483
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:43,881
"They go play"?

484
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:58,145
<i>They play doctor.</i>

485
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:02,817
They said no. I can't.

486
00:40:05,277 --> 00:40:06,278
I see.

487
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:11,742
Well, some kids get nightmares,
and can't sleep well when it's lights-out.

488
00:40:12,576 --> 00:40:15,913
They say Baba reassures them
so they can sleep, they feel safe.

489
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:17,415
Really?

490
00:40:18,207 --> 00:40:19,041
What?

491
00:40:20,376 --> 00:40:22,169
- Oh, nothing.
- Hmm.

492
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:26,799
Ah, we raised a lot of money
with our last push,

493
00:40:26,882 --> 00:40:29,218
so we can buy the medical supplies
we're short on.

494
00:40:29,301 --> 00:40:30,719
Everyone likes it here.

495
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:32,847
These poor kids have
nowhere else they can go.

496
00:40:51,574 --> 00:40:54,076
So, is there someplace else we could go?

497
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:56,287
What do you mean, you don't like it here?

498
00:40:56,370 --> 00:40:57,663
I don't know.

499
00:40:57,746 --> 00:41:01,208
Another place, or anything
that we can try and go to, is there?

500
00:41:04,336 --> 00:41:05,546
Baba!

501
00:41:05,629 --> 00:41:06,964
Baba!

502
00:41:07,047 --> 00:41:09,258
- Come sit with me, Baba.
- How are you?

503
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:10,342
Hi, Baba!

504
00:41:10,426 --> 00:41:12,553
- How are you, sweetie?
- Mmm.

505
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:46,504
Oh, we're on patrol duty today, right?

506
00:41:46,587 --> 00:41:49,006
Sleep a little longer.
I'll go to the clinic, don't worry.

507
00:41:49,089 --> 00:41:51,217
Oh, no, no. Oh.

508
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,718
Oh, gosh.

509
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:54,512
- Ah.
- It's all right.

510
00:41:56,555 --> 00:42:00,559
Oh, man. Why does my body feel so heavy?

511
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:05,481
I hope these are his size.

512
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:07,149
I'm sure they'll fit great.

513
00:42:07,233 --> 00:42:09,693
You went through
so much trouble to get them.

514
00:42:09,777 --> 00:42:14,281
Su-jeong, hey,
30 more minutes and I'll join you.

515
00:42:23,249 --> 00:42:25,584
Shh! Shh!

516
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:32,883
Baraka and Neema, where could you be?

517
00:42:56,448 --> 00:42:58,450
Neema.

518
00:42:59,785 --> 00:43:00,953
Neema!

519
00:43:02,496 --> 00:43:03,622
Neema!

520
00:43:40,659 --> 00:43:41,660
Baraka.

521
00:43:43,787 --> 00:43:44,788
Neema?

522
00:45:11,959 --> 00:45:13,752
<i>Is Baba good?</i>

523
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:15,295
A good person?

524
00:45:23,595 --> 00:45:24,722
Oh, God.

525
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:28,267
So, is there someplace else we could go?

526
00:45:29,184 --> 00:45:31,270
<i>What do you mean? You don't like it here?</i>

527
00:45:31,353 --> 00:45:32,730
<i>I don't know.</i>

528
00:45:32,813 --> 00:45:36,150
<i>Another place, or anything</i>
<i>that we can try and go to, is there?</i>

529
00:46:15,272 --> 00:46:17,441
- Out! Everyone out, out!
- Careful!

530
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:19,777
Neema! Baraka!

531
00:46:21,528 --> 00:46:24,156
Neema! Baraka!

532
00:46:26,492 --> 00:46:29,453
Baraka! Neema!

533
00:46:30,204 --> 00:46:31,872
Baraka!

534
00:46:34,249 --> 00:46:35,375
Neema!

535
00:46:36,835 --> 00:46:39,213
Miss Teacher, please…

536
00:46:39,838 --> 00:46:41,048
Let's go outside.

537
00:46:48,931 --> 00:46:49,932
Su-jeong!

538
00:46:54,645 --> 00:46:57,231
Okay. Where's Baraka?

539
00:46:57,314 --> 00:46:58,732
Neema, where is Baraka?

540
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:21,880
I'll start a fire. Really.
Don't make me do it.

541
00:47:21,964 --> 00:47:23,799
Teacher, please. Leave us alone.

542
00:47:23,882 --> 00:47:25,425
I want it to stop.

543
00:47:25,509 --> 00:47:28,554
Oh… Poor little Baraka.

544
00:47:39,481 --> 00:47:42,568
Neema. You're still outside the door?

545
00:47:47,990 --> 00:47:49,783
Neema! Run!

546
00:47:51,827 --> 00:47:54,204
Baraka!

547
00:48:02,045 --> 00:48:03,255
Baraka!

548
00:48:14,725 --> 00:48:15,726
Baraka!

549
00:48:17,811 --> 00:48:20,480
Baraka! Baraka!

550
00:48:33,160 --> 00:48:34,161
Baraka!

551
00:48:45,505 --> 00:48:47,841
Ah!

552
00:49:07,319 --> 00:49:08,570
Wait…

553
00:49:33,261 --> 00:49:34,721
No.

554
00:49:48,402 --> 00:49:49,403
Baraka.

555
00:49:52,239 --> 00:49:54,282
One, two, three, four.

556
00:49:54,366 --> 00:49:55,367
Baraka.

557
00:49:58,954 --> 00:50:00,372
One, two, three, four.

558
00:50:12,467 --> 00:50:14,803
Baraka. Baraka?

559
00:50:15,804 --> 00:50:16,805
Wake up.

560
00:50:18,306 --> 00:50:19,516
Baraka.

561
00:50:57,387 --> 00:50:58,930
<i>No matter how long </i>I <i>wait…</i>

562
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:01,975
No!

563
00:51:04,770 --> 00:51:07,064
<i>Baraka doesn't appear in my dreams.</i>

564
00:51:22,954 --> 00:51:26,333
<i>For me, that's the most painful part.</i>

565
00:51:26,416 --> 00:51:29,002
We got rid of anything
that might be a concern.

566
00:51:29,086 --> 00:51:30,170
The children…

567
00:51:30,754 --> 00:51:33,548
Yes, we're still looking
for Neema right now.

568
00:51:34,341 --> 00:51:37,427
We'll take care of things.
No harm will come to you, Baba.

569
00:51:50,107 --> 00:51:55,153
<i>I asked Mi-gyeong for her help</i>
<i>to find you a good temporary foster home.</i>

570
00:51:56,029 --> 00:51:57,364
<i>And, after that…</i>

571
00:51:58,990 --> 00:52:00,158
<i>I ran away.</i>

572
00:52:01,284 --> 00:52:02,619
<i>To somewhere else.</i>

573
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:09,417
You're next.

574
00:52:17,717 --> 00:52:20,303
I'm repaying you
for saving my life all those years ago.

575
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:22,013
It was nice seeing you again
after so long.

576
00:52:22,097 --> 00:52:24,182
- You're welcome here anytime.
- <i>But…</i>

577
00:52:24,933 --> 00:52:27,310
<i>Dr. Jang Hui-suk never gave up on me.</i>

578
00:52:37,070 --> 00:52:38,738
Let's go home, Su-jeong.

579
00:52:39,614 --> 00:52:40,615
<i>Home…</i>

580
00:52:41,700 --> 00:52:43,743
<i>Is that a place I deserve to be?</i>

581
00:52:45,162 --> 00:52:48,790
<i>Do I have the right to eat</i>
<i>and regain my strength?</i>

582
00:52:51,251 --> 00:52:52,252
Here.

583
00:52:58,049 --> 00:53:00,260
Do you think I don't know you want to die?

584
00:53:00,343 --> 00:53:02,470
And do you really think
I would let you die?

585
00:53:04,514 --> 00:53:07,142
Come on, eat a little, come on.

586
00:53:08,977 --> 00:53:10,979
Open, you gotta eat. Huh?

587
00:53:15,901 --> 00:53:16,902
Auntie.

588
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:20,864
You and I…

589
00:53:22,699 --> 00:53:26,244
rescued that man… and he got to live.

590
00:53:30,123 --> 00:53:31,208
What?

591
00:53:31,291 --> 00:53:32,334
We…

592
00:53:33,710 --> 00:53:35,337
saved that person's life…

593
00:53:39,382 --> 00:53:40,592
and celebrated.

594
00:53:42,886 --> 00:53:47,057
We… were glad he could go on…

595
00:53:49,768 --> 00:53:50,769
to live.

596
00:53:54,981 --> 00:53:59,402
We… let that man back into the world…

597
00:54:01,488 --> 00:54:03,573
and just stood there cheering!

598
00:54:13,083 --> 00:54:14,084
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

599
00:54:17,337 --> 00:54:19,798
<i>I'm sorry for saving that person's life.</i>

600
00:54:19,881 --> 00:54:22,592
<i>I'm sorry for saving that person's life,</i>

601
00:54:22,676 --> 00:54:25,428
<i>smiling, and being happy about it.</i>

602
00:54:25,512 --> 00:54:27,055
<i>I'm sorry I didn't know.</i>

603
00:54:27,973 --> 00:54:29,933
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't save Baraka.</i>

604
00:54:30,475 --> 00:54:32,227
Hey, Su-jeong, come on, please eat.

605
00:54:33,436 --> 00:54:35,772
- Just a little more. Open up, honey.
<i>- I'm sorry.</i>

606
00:54:35,855 --> 00:54:38,149
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

607
00:54:38,233 --> 00:54:40,277
<i>I'm sorry for still being alive.</i>

608
00:54:46,700 --> 00:54:49,703
The mail's here. Neema sent you a letter.

609
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:56,001
She says she's settled into the new place
and she's doing well.

610
00:54:58,837 --> 00:54:59,963
A letter?

611
00:55:00,964 --> 00:55:02,841
That means Neema…

612
00:55:02,924 --> 00:55:06,803
I heard she learned to read.
And it looks like she can write now.

613
00:55:18,773 --> 00:55:20,525
She sent this over also…

614
00:55:21,609 --> 00:55:22,777
to protect you.

615
00:55:52,599 --> 00:55:54,809
Whoa, whoa, hey, you. Uh, I, I…

616
00:55:54,893 --> 00:55:56,936
- Ms. Jang!
- <i>Blessings and grace.</i>

617
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:59,606
<i>- Baraka and Neema.</i>
- Come down here! She got into the eggs!

618
00:55:59,689 --> 00:56:00,940
<i>My friends.</i>

619
00:56:01,691 --> 00:56:03,276
<i>My saviors.</i>

620
00:56:04,652 --> 00:56:05,862
Uh, Dr. Gye?

621
00:56:05,945 --> 00:56:08,907
Uh… Just for me, uh, could you…

622
00:56:09,991 --> 00:56:12,535
Uh, can you please just fail this once?

623
00:56:13,411 --> 00:56:14,454
Please.

624
00:56:53,284 --> 00:56:55,120
Do you have dreams as well?

625
00:56:57,664 --> 00:56:59,124
Nightmares.

626
00:57:13,555 --> 00:57:14,973
You were still…

627
00:57:18,351 --> 00:57:19,644
alone then.

628
00:57:57,056 --> 00:58:01,269
<i>I intend, once again, to save this person.</i>

629
00:58:09,819 --> 00:58:10,820
<i>A monster…</i>

630
00:58:11,529 --> 00:58:13,740
<i>who, in the flames…</i>

631
00:58:13,823 --> 00:58:16,326
<i>pressed Baraka against his face</i>

632
00:58:16,409 --> 00:58:18,495
<i>and used him to shield himself.</i>

633
00:58:20,830 --> 00:58:23,124
<i>The monster who stole your voice.</i>

634
00:58:30,798 --> 00:58:32,592
<i>I intend to save him.</i>

635
00:58:46,272 --> 00:58:49,984
<i>And, after… with his new beating heart,</i>

636
00:58:50,610 --> 00:58:52,820
<i>he'll prowl around children once more,</i>

637
00:58:53,446 --> 00:58:55,990
<i>and all his little zealots</i>
<i>will cover for him.</i>

638
00:58:57,033 --> 00:58:59,077
<i>Until finally, one day,</i>

639
00:58:59,702 --> 00:59:03,540
<i>he will pass away peacefully,</i>
<i>amid respect, and praise…</i>

640
00:59:03,623 --> 00:59:04,958
<i>and tears.</i>

641
00:59:05,833 --> 00:59:09,420
<i>But, that's… too easy, isn't it?</i>

642
00:59:10,380 --> 00:59:13,633
<i>That's far too… comfortable.</i>

643
00:59:14,551 --> 00:59:16,344
PATIENT NAME
KIM SEUNG-HYO

644
00:59:56,426 --> 01:00:00,013
All right. Moment of silence.

645
01:00:02,932 --> 01:00:05,435
May the decision of
the donor and their family

646
01:00:05,518 --> 01:00:07,437
not be the end, but a beginning…

647
01:00:07,520 --> 01:00:09,272
<i>My last patient.</i>

648
01:00:09,355 --> 01:00:10,982
Yes. Understood.

649
01:00:13,109 --> 01:00:14,569
Donor, anesthetic…

650
01:00:14,652 --> 01:00:16,070
<i>My last surgery.</i>

651
01:00:16,738 --> 01:00:18,281
The donor's induction has begun.

652
01:00:19,699 --> 01:00:21,117
Let's begin the surgery.

653
01:00:38,176 --> 01:00:40,762
As expected, there's adhesion
with the second surgery…

654
01:00:41,554 --> 01:00:43,765
Keep me in the loop
so the timing lines up.

655
01:00:43,848 --> 01:00:44,849
Will do, Doctor.

656
01:00:45,975 --> 01:00:49,145
Oh, Dr. Jo, you're playing music today?
How unusual.

657
01:00:49,729 --> 01:00:50,730
Mmm.

658
01:00:50,813 --> 01:00:54,901
The patient wanted to have his favorite
sounds playing during his operation.

659
01:01:25,473 --> 01:01:27,266
Oh? Dad!

660
01:01:28,226 --> 01:01:29,644
Hello, Mister.

661
01:01:31,270 --> 01:01:33,481
<i>Bringing the children's nightmares,</i>

662
01:01:35,483 --> 01:01:36,984
<i>screams,</i>

663
01:01:48,037 --> 01:01:49,038
<i>and pain…</i>

664
01:01:52,750 --> 01:01:54,043
<i>to your bed.</i>

665
01:02:14,230 --> 01:02:19,360
A DRUG THAT WAKES THE PATIENT BY REVERSING
THE EFFECTS OF A SPECIFIC SEDATIVE

666
01:02:19,444 --> 01:02:21,529
<i>You can no longer sleep in peace.</i>

667
01:02:31,581 --> 01:02:33,916
<i>This is your hell.</i>

668
01:02:35,793 --> 01:02:38,087
I will start the dissection. Bovie.

669
01:04:00,127 --> 01:04:03,047
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

670
01:04:42,169 --> 01:04:45,089
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

671
01:04:45,172 --> 01:04:47,550
<i>He's just not that kind of person.</i>

672
01:04:48,217 --> 01:04:50,511
However, I'm not him.

673
01:04:50,595 --> 01:04:53,014
The hospital's being shut down.

674
01:04:53,097 --> 01:04:54,098
Shit!

675
01:04:54,181 --> 01:04:56,642
<i>Somehow, we both survived</i>

676
01:04:56,726 --> 01:04:58,227
<i>and made it this far.</i>

677
01:04:59,145 --> 01:05:00,771
You're done with being doctors after this!

678
01:05:00,855 --> 01:05:02,356
Do you believe in God?

679
01:05:03,107 --> 01:05:04,442
I hate Him.

680
01:05:05,318 --> 01:05:06,861
The surgery…

681
01:05:07,445 --> 01:05:08,946
will be stopped.
